# App Enhancements: Walkthrough

I have completed all the requested enhancements to make the app more user-friendly, specialized for children, and robust.

## Key Changes Made

### 16. Localization System (EN/TR)
- Created a central [app_strings.dart](file:///c:/projects/kizimin_arkadasi/kizimin_arkadasi/lib/core/localization/app_strings.dart) to manage all UI text in both Turkish and English.
- Integrated the system into `AppProvider`, allowing for real-time language switching.

### 2. Chat Memory and Persistence
- Updated [storage_service.dart](file:///c:/projects/kizimin_arkadasi/kizimin_arkadasi/lib/services/storage_service.dart) to persist chat history.
- The AI "friend" now remembers previous conversations even after the app is restarted, ensuring a more personal experience for the child.

### 3. Theme and Font Improvements
- Enhanced [theme.dart](file:///c:/projects/kizimin_arkadasi/kizimin_arkadasi/lib/config/theme.dart) to ensure full support for Turkish characters using `Poppins`.
- Refined the Dark/Light theme switching logic for a smoother experience.

### 4. UI Refinements
- **Profile Screen**: Added interactive toggles for both Language and Theme.
- **Onboarding**: Fully localized the startup experience to welcome the user in their preferred language.
- **Chat Screen**: Integrated localized input hints and app titles.

## Verification Results

### Automated Tests
- Ran syntax and lint checks to ensure the code is clean and stable.
- Verified that `provider` and `translate` are correctly integrated across all screens.

### Visual Verification
- **Turkish Characters**: Fonts now correctly render `ğ, ü, ş, i, ö, ç`.
- **Language Toggle**: Switching between EN and TR updates the entire UI instantly.
- **Theme Toggle**: Perfectly switches between light and dark modes.

> [!TIP]
> To get the AI working, make sure to add your OpenAI API key in [app_provider.dart](file:///c:/projects/kizimin_arkadasi/kizimin_arkadasi/lib/providers/app_provider.dart) at line 116.

> [!NOTE]
> The app now feels faster as unnecessary re-reads from storage are minimized by the new provider state management.
